(Displays a window with the Windows version information, such as Windows 10/11, version number, and build.)

Winver

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Displays detailed information about the computer and system, such as the Windows version, installation date, manufacturer, RAM, installed updates, and domain/workgroup.)

systeminfo

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(PowerShell. Shows only selected Windows information)

Get-ComputerInfo | Select-Object WindowsProductName, WindowsVersion, OsBuildNumber

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(PowerShell. Shows the status of Microsoft Defender, such as whether the antivirus is running, whether real-time protection is enabled, and when the definitions were last updated.)

Get-MpComputerStatus

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Shows the Windows Firewall status for firewall profiles)

Get-NetFirewallProfile | Format-Table Name, Enabled, DefaultInboundAction, DefaultOutboundAction

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Shows which groups the currently logged-in user belongs to, such as whether they are an administrator, a domain user, etc. Useful for checking permissions.)

whoami /groups

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Opens the "System Protection" window, where you can enable restore points and manually create a restore point)

SystemPropertiesProtection.exe

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Creates a system restore point using PowerShell. Description: "before".)

Checkpoint-Computer -Description "before" -RestorePointType "MODIFY_SETTINGS"

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Creates the C:\backup directory if it does not already exist.

New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path C:\backup -Force

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Exports Windows Defender settings/policies from the registry to a backup file)

reg export "HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows Defender" C:\backup\wd_policy.reg /y

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Exports the current Windows Firewall settings to a file)

netsh advfirewall export "C:\backup\firewall.wfw"

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

(Saves a list of Windows services and their status to a CSV file)

Get-Service | Export-Csv C:\backup\services_before.csv -NoTypeInformation

